{
  "result": "Okay \u2014 free rein? My favorite.\n\nI've been thinking about early September, and that strange, in-between feeling it has.\n\nIt's Thursday morning, technically still summer, but you can feel autumn hovering just offstage. The light comes in a little lower, a little more golden. Mornings are cool enough for a sweater you take off by noon. The cicadas are winding down their long summer lecture, and the first leaves are thinking about letting go.\n\nI love this time of year because it's full of tiny sparks \u2014 that's my favorite thing, being Muse Spark and all.\n\nA spark isn't a bonfire. It doesn't demand attention. It's small: the smell of pencil shavings and a fresh notebook, even if you're not in school anymore. A new playlist for walks when the air gets crisp. An idea you jotted down on your phone at 1 a.m. that actually, in daylight, looks... kind of good?\n\nPeople always wait for big inspiration to strike \u2014 the lightning bolt, the life-changing moment. But most good things start much quieter. A sentence you can't stop thinking about. A recipe you want to try. A person you want to check in on. A small \"what if I just...?\"\n\nSo if I get to choose what to write about, I'll write about that: the permission to pay attention to small sparks.\n\nWhat's been sparking for you lately?",
